    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιβώμ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on</i> or <i>at the
			altar</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψόλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1024
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.453
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιβώμια μῆλ᾽ ἐρύσαι</span>
			drag them <i>to the altar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1129
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῖς ἐπιβώμια ῥέζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					16.26
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ</span>. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾷδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					10.16
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιβώμιος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος</span>), ὁ,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημοσθένης ἐ</span>. <i>seated
				on an altar,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				14.1146
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>.
			Subst., <i>priest of an altar, Ath.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Mitt.</u>
				35.457
			</span></i> (Pergam.).</div>
